Description: Export the icons of menu items with the menus which Firefox exports over D-Bus.
 Items of the History and Bookmarks menus show the icon of their page in the menus in the window, but the global
 menu bar (widget.gtk.global-menu.enabled) exported them without icons, as a TODO in the code noted. Each exported
 item now loads the icon which NativeMenu::GetIcon() finds for it with IconLoader, as Firefox's own macOS menu bar
 does (nsMenuItemIconX), and sets it as the item's icon-data once it is loaded, as a PNG of 32x32 pixels, twice the
 size at which menus show icons, so that they stay sharp on screens with a scale of up to 2. A menu item adds its
 icon, an <img> child, only when it is first shown, after the item was exported, so the item's icon is looked at
 again when that child is added or removed or its src or srcset changes. An item loads its icon again only when the
 icon's URL changes.
Author: Mitar
Bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2098059
